  "routerErrorAnalysis": {
    "derivation": [
      "Upstream order: logits = F.linear(x, W); p = softmax(logits, dtype=float32, dim=-1) over all 512 experts; v, idx = topk(p, 10); v /= v.sum(-1, keepdim=True); v.to(float32). Sigmoid is not used by this router; it gates only the shared expert.",
      "Logits: |fl(x.w_e) - x.w_e| <= gamma_n * sum_i |x_i w_ei|, n = 2560, gamma_n = n*u/(1-n*u), u = 2^-24, for any summation order with or without FMA (Higham, Accuracy and Stability, eq. 3.5). Requires float32 matmul precision \"highest\".",
      "Softmax (PyTorch _vec_softmax_lastdim for float): m = max (exact); E_j = exp(fl(l_j - m)) with fl(l_j - m) = (l_j - m)(1+a), |a| <= u, and exp relative error <= C_EXP*u; Z = sum E_j and R = fl(1/Z) are common to the row; p_j = fl(E_j * R), one rounding.",
      "Renormalization cancels the common Z and R exactly: v_i = E_i(1+r_i)(1+d_i) / sum_S E_j(1+r_j)(1+t_j), |t_j| <= gamma_{k-1} for the 10-term sum in any order, |d_i| <= u for the final division. In exact arithmetic v_i = exp(l_i)/sum_S exp(l_j), so the exact reference is softmax over the retained exact logits.",
      "With beta_j the logit bound and L(t) = -log(1-t): |log(v_i/s_i)| <= N_i + D, N_i = beta_i + u|l_i - m| + L(C_EXP u) + 2 L(u), D = max_S(beta_j + u|l_j - m|) + L(C_EXP u) + L(u) + L(gamma_{k-1}); hence |v_i - s_i| <= s_i * expm1(N_i + D).",
      "Selection is provably the exact top-k when min_S(l_j - beta_j - u|l_j - m|) - max_notS(l_k + beta_k + u|l_k - m|) - 2 L(C_EXP u) - 2 L(u) > 0.",
      "Each bound is multiplied by (1 + 2^-40) for its own float64 evaluation and allows 16 * 2^-53 relative error in the float64 truth."
    ],
